<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3731"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Pax56<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Pax56<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, January 07, 2005 - 9:17 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->You&#39;re absolutely right.  The prostitution angle is the one part of his new confessions I don&#39;t question much.  I&#39;ll bet he likes it strange.  Prostitutes were probably the closest he could get to his fantasies without committing a felony.  He seems never to have gone &#34;all the way&#34; with prostitutes, unless there were a lot of dead hookers turning up in Wichita &#40;or wherever he was in the 90&#39;s&#41;.  If the &#39;Nam thing holds true, we might be looking for a military or bondage fetish of some kind - might have even brought his bowling bag full of goodies.  Any places in Wichita that specialize in the strange guys?  I&#39;ll bet he was running a tab there, wherever it was.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
