<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6418"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 07, 2005 - 12:04 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->After thinking it over, I don&#39;t believe BTK used prostitutes. With the exception of specific clues to prove he committed a given murder, I believe BTK usually lied. All sociopaths lie, it&#39;s the most overt characteristic they share. BTK is image-conscious, as the Otero letter demonstrates; BTK opines that he&#39;ll be called &#34;psychotic with sexual perversion hang-up.&#34; <i>Why</i> would BTK write this? &#34;Psychotic with sexual perversion hang-up&#34; isn&#39;t exactly a diagnostic clinical term, so why? It may represent more than one thing, but I see a BTK who is concerned with how he is perceived by newspaper-reading Wichitans.  <BR> <BR>Something else. BTK refers to masturbation with some frequency. No serial killer has raised this topic in any letter. Even Zodiac, when graphic, wrote &#34;it&#39;s even better than getting your rocks off with <i>a girl.</i>&#34; <b>Zodiac took the time to include this information in a sophisticated cryptogram, so it was obviously important to him - probably <i>crucial</i> to him - that he be thought of as a typical,</b> heterosexual, cool guy who has a penchant for murdering young couples. Now, BTK heavily references masturbation and pornography in the Otero letter. Vian letter, too. Why? In my opinion, the chief reason is to shock the reader. <BR> <BR>He&#39;s mentioning things which many, especially in 1974, would consider unsavory or even depraved - particularly in conservative Kansas. I see a plausible attempt to imply he solicited prostitutes in this very letter, albeit in a very oblique way - when refering to future victims. Prostitutes, commonly, are victims. In the 11/2004 jumble of non sequiturs, the phrase &#34;he admits to having solicted prostitutes&#34; is observed. Many think this a hint that BTK has murdered at least one prostitute or that prostitutes in Wichita need only be questioned and perhaps that&#39;s the break we&#39;ve been waiting for. These thoughts are perfectly sound but I respectfully disagree with them.  <BR> <BR>I think BTK has a <i>need</i> to be perceived as being capable of coitus, even if it means coitus with prostitutes. Nothing from the crime scene information indicates BTK was capable of coitus. Using known serial killer data, BTK would have first murdered, and then satisfied himself when next to the bodies. It was the only way he could achieve sexual gratification. This was also true of Jeffrey Dahmer and John Wayne Gacy, to name just two. <BR> <BR>It boils down to sexual dysfunction, IMO. My definition of sexual dysfunction in BTK&#39;s case is merely that BTK couldn&#39;t achieve or maintain an erection with a live person. He had to kill them first. As BTK is nearly incapable of telling the truth, and because I believe him incapable of coitus due to sexual dysfunction, I don&#39;t believe BTK has ever been with a prostitute, although his ego demands that he be perceived as capable of basic sex with grown women. <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
